body:
COACHING SUBMISSION T25: New MCM Component -- Question Position Tracker
Designed from scratch with every decision annotated.

---

COMPONENT: Sticky Question Position Indicator
The component that does not yet exist in MCM.

WHAT IT IS
A minimal sticky bar at the top of the exam that shows Kai's current position in the question stack: "Q3 of 15" -- updating as she scrolls.

WHY THIS COMPONENT (not a different one)
T18 identified the post-wrong-answer transition as the highest ADHD risk point. After a wrong answer, Kai loses orientation in the scroll. The position tracker gives a persistent anchor. She does not need to scroll up to count, hold the count in working memory, or wonder how many questions are left. It is always visible, always current.

---

EVERY DECISION, ANNOTATED

PLACEMENT: sticky top, full width
Decision: top of viewport, not bottom.
Why: Kai's natural scanning direction is top-to-bottom. If the tracker is at the bottom of the screen, it requires an eye movement counter to her reading direction. At the top, it is in peripheral vision during question-reading and does not compete for focus.
Alt considered: floating bottom-right badge (common in some quiz UIs). Rejected: occupies right side of screen where scroll thumb lives, competes with scrollbar visual.

SIZE: font-size var(--text-sm), 14px
Decision: smallest body size, not xs.
Why: the tracker is reference information, not primary content. --text-sm at 14px is readable without magnification but does not compete with question text (--text-base 16px). xs (12px) is too small to read in peripheral vision reliably.

COLOR: --text-secondary on --bg-page (or bg-card in arena)
Decision: use --text-secondary, not --text-primary.
Why: This information is always true, always visible. If it were --text-primary it would fight with question text. Secondary color signals "this is ambient information" not "this needs your immediate attention." In arena mode: --text-secondary (#8B92A8) on --bg-card (#141B2D) = 5.53:1 PASS.

BACKGROUND: same as --bg-page, no border, 8px bottom shadow
Decision: no contrasting background color on the tracker bar.
Why: a colored bar would fragment the exam into two distinct visual zones (nav vs. content). The shadow provides visual separation without a hard edge. This follows the design system's shadow-card convention.
Shadow value: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.15) -- slightly heavier than --shadow-card because this element floats above content.

FORMAT: "Q3 of 15" not "Question 3/15" or "3/15"
Decision: abbreviated with spelled-out "of."
Why: "Q3" is scannable in <100ms. "of 15" gives scope context. "3/15" is ambiguous (ratio? fraction? score?). The format is unambiguous and minimal.
Copy rule: always "Q[N] of [total]" -- no "Question" prefix, no em dash, no parentheses.

ANIMATION: IntersectionObserver, updates instantly (no transition)
Decision: instant update, no fade/slide.
Why: the position number changing slowly would draw Kai's attention every time she scrolls past a question. Instant update reads as passive reference, not notification. Any animation here competes with the actual content.
prefers-reduced-motion: no change needed (no animation to remove).

Z-INDEX: 100
Decision: above all question content, below modal overlays.
Why: must stay visible while Kai scrolls through card content. z-index 100 is below any hypothetical overlay (z-index 200+). Does not require z-index fighting with Card.js chart canvases (which are z-index: auto).

EDGE CASE: picker mode (no exam loaded)
Decision: do not render the tracker if examData is null or questions array is empty.
Why: the picker screen has no questions to track. The tracker div should exist in the DOM but have display:none until loadExam() fires.

EDGE CASE: single-question exam (N of 1)
Decision: still render "Q1 of 1" -- do not hide it.
Why: future-proofing. If Marcus adds a 1-question drill, the tracker is accurate. Hiding it for edge cases adds conditional logic for no user benefit.

---

IMPLEMENTATION NOTES FOR GA
HTML: add above questionsContainer: <div id="questionTracker" style="display:none;">Q1 of 1</div>
CSS in shared/styles.css:
  #questionTracker {
    position: sticky;
    top: 0;
    z-index: 100;
    padding: 6px 16px;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    background: var(--bg-page);
    box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.15);
    text-align: right;
  }
JS after loadExam():
  var questions = examData.questions;
  var tracker = document.getElementById('questionTracker');
  tracker.textContent = 'Q1 of ' + questions.length;
  tracker.style.display = '';
  var qEls = questionsContainer.querySelectorAll('.question-block');
  var io = new IntersectionObserver(function(entries) {
    entries.forEach(function(e) {
      if (e.isIntersecting) {
        var idx = Array.prototype.indexOf.call(qEls, e.target);
        tracker.textContent = 'Q' + (idx+1) + ' of ' + questions.length;
      }
    });
  }, { rootMargin: '-30% 0px -60% 0px' });
  qEls.forEach(function(el) { io.observe(el); });
